    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Livelihood opportunities for 7,516 HHs
&#x2022;	16 Partnership and Co-funding with Local governments
&#x2022;	70% women participation
&#x2022;	60 Hectare of riverbed rehabilitation and cultivation with agroforestry and multilayer plantation
&#x2022;	20 Green and Resilient Infrastructure development</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	8,178 HHs enhanced livelihood opportunities through green jobs which directly benefit to 45,751 people.
&#x2022;	Partnership is established with 16 local governments under co-funding modality.
&#x2022;	64 hectares of riverbed land rehabilitated and cultivated with agroforestry and multilayer plantation.
&#x2022;	71.42% of women participation, 15.5% Dalits, 35.5 Indigenous nationalities, 5% Madhesi, 13.64% Returnee migrants.
&#x2022;	24 green and resilient infrastructure developed.
&#x2022;	644 small infrastructures developed.
&#x2022;	14 types of plants with 25,337 saplings plantations took a place.
&#x2022;	34 types of 49,745 Agriculture tools, technology and equipment supported.
&#x2022;	Over 2,500 short term jobs creation.
&#x2022;	86.65 million NPR income is possible as of the date by the project (including 2075 tons of agri production, n 91 commodities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
